Rem ==================================================================
Rem seedxml.shoddy — reckoner seed: xml.shoddy, converting at the
Rem bridge
Rem
Rem XMLPARSE, XMLTEXT, XMLPRETTY, XMLLOAD and XMLSAVE. Per R4.16 there
Rem is no TREE cell at the keyboard: an Xml node converts to a tagged
Rem LIST — { "elem" tag attrs kids }, { "comment" text } and so on, one
Rem shape per Xml case — except XText, which is exactly as much as a
Rem STRING already is and travels as one. XcOfXml/XcToXml are the
Rem whole bridge, and seedhtml.shoddy Includes this file to reuse them
Rem rather than duplicate the tree shape for a second machine that
Rem answers the same Xml type.
Rem
Rem AN ELEMENT'S ATTRIBUTES ARE A DICT, the same LIST-of-PAIR shape
Rem seeddict.shoddy already established — DGET/DHAS/DKEYS read an
Rem element's attrs unchanged.
Rem
Rem XMLLOAD and XMLSAVE go through TRYREADFILE/TRYWRITEFILE rather than
Rem xml.shoddy's own XmlLoad/XmlSave, which are built on the aborting
Rem ReadFile/WriteFile (R3.5(a)). XMLPARSE reads through XmlRead, the
Rem total half of XmlParse, for the same reason.
Rem ==================================================================

Include "xml.shoddy"
Include "cuttle.shoddy"
Include "reckoner.shoddy"
Include "seq.shoddy"

Rem ---- Xml <-> Cell, at the bridge -------------------------------------

Rem Total: every Xml case has a cell shape, XText's the plainest of all.
Def XcToXml(x As Xml) As Cell
    Select Case x
        Case XText(t)
            CutStr(t)
        Case XDocument(ns)
            CutList({ CutStr("document"), CutList(Map(ns, XcToXml)) })
        Case XComment(b)
            CutList({ CutStr("comment"), CutStr(b) })
        Case XCData(r)
            CutList({ CutStr("cdata"), CutStr(r) })
        Case XDoctype(dtd)
            CutList({ CutStr("doctype"), CutStr(dtd) })
        Case XPI(t, dat)
            CutList({ CutStr("pi"), CutStr(t), CutStr(dat) })
        Case XElem(tag, attrs, kids)
            CutList({ CutStr("elem"), CutStr(tag), CutList(Map(attrs, XcAttrOf)), CutList(Map(kids, XcToXml)) })
        Case Else
            CutStr("")

Def XcAttrOf(p As Pair) As Cell
    CutPair(Pair(CutStr(Fst(p)), CutStr(Snd(p))))

Rem The other direction. A malformed tagged list — the wrong length, a
Rem kind this bridge does not know — reads back as an empty text node
Rem rather than refusing: XMLTEXT and XMLPRETTY are RckPure and R3.5(a)
Rem means neither can abort on a hand-built list that got the shape
Rem wrong, so the least surprising total answer is silence, not a tree
Rem missing its writer entirely.
Def XcOfXml(c As Cell) As Xml
    Select Case c
        Case CutStr(t)
            XText(t)
        Case CutList(xs)
            XcOfList(xs)
        Case Else
            XText("")

Def XcOfList(xs As List Of Cell) As Xml
    If IsEmpty(xs) Then
        XText("")
    Else
        XcOfKinded(First(xs), Rest(xs))

Def XcOfKinded(kind As Cell, rest As List Of Cell) As Xml
    Select Case kind
        Case CutStr(k)
            XcOfNamed(k, rest)
        Case Else
            XText("")

Def XcOfNamed(k As String, rest As List Of Cell) As Xml
    If k = "document" Then
        XcOfDocument(rest)
    Else
        If k = "comment" Then
            XcOfComment(rest)
        Else
            If k = "cdata" Then
                XcOfCdata(rest)
            Else
                If k = "doctype" Then
                    XcOfDoctype(rest)
                Else
                    If k = "pi" Then
                        XcOfPi(rest)
                    Else
                        If k = "elem" Then
                            XcOfElem(rest)
                        Else
                            XText("")

Def XcOfDocument(rest As List Of Cell) As Xml
    Select Case First(rest)
        Case CutList(ns)
            XDocument(Map(ns, XcOfXml))
        Case Else
            XText("")

Def XcOfComment(rest As List Of Cell) As Xml
    Select Case First(rest)
        Case CutStr(b)
            XComment(b)
        Case Else
            XText("")

Def XcOfCdata(rest As List Of Cell) As Xml
    Select Case First(rest)
        Case CutStr(r)
            XCData(r)
        Case Else
            XText("")

Def XcOfDoctype(rest As List Of Cell) As Xml
    Select Case First(rest)
        Case CutStr(dtd)
            XDoctype(dtd)
        Case Else
            XText("")

Def XcOfPi(rest As List Of Cell) As Xml
    If Length(rest) < 2 Then
        XText("")
    Else
        XcOfPiVals(Nth(rest, 1), Nth(rest, 2))

Def XcOfPiVals(t As Cell, dat As Cell) As Xml
    Select Case Pair(t, dat)
        Case Pair(CutStr(ts), CutStr(ds))
            XPI(ts, ds)
        Case Else
            XText("")

Def XcOfElem(rest As List Of Cell) As Xml
    If Length(rest) < 3 Then
        XText("")
    Else
        XcOfElemVals(Nth(rest, 1), Nth(rest, 2), Nth(rest, 3))

Def XcOfElemVals(tag As Cell, attrs As Cell, kids As Cell) As Xml
    Select Case tag
        Case CutStr(ts)
            XcOfElemAttrs(ts, attrs, kids)
        Case Else
            XText("")

Def XcOfElemAttrs(tag As String, attrs As Cell, kids As Cell) As Xml
    Select Case attrs
        Case CutList(al)
            XcOfElemKids(tag, Map(al, XcAttrPair), kids)
        Case Else
            XText("")

Def XcAttrPair(c As Cell) As Pair
    Select Case c
        Case CutPair(p)
            XcAttrPairOf(Fst(p), Snd(p))
        Case Else
            Pair("", "")

Def XcAttrPairOf(k As Cell, v As Cell) As Pair
    Select Case Pair(k, v)
        Case Pair(CutStr(ks), CutStr(vs))
            Pair(ks, vs)
        Case Else
            Pair("", "")

Def XcOfElemKids(tag As String, attrs As List Of Pair, kids As Cell) As Xml
    Select Case kids
        Case CutList(kl)
            XElem(tag, attrs, Map(kl, XcOfXml))
        Case Else
            XText("")

Rem ---- XMLPARSE -----------------------------------------------------------

Def XsSeedXmlparse(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "XMLPARSE", 1, RckPure(Fn(vs) => XsXmlparse(vs)), "( str -- doc )", "The string, parsed as XML — an element is { \"elem\" tag attrs kids }, attrs a dict.")

Def XsXmlparse(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckTextArg("XMLPARSE", First(vs))
        Case Ok(s)
            XsXmlparseRead(XmlRead(s))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("XMLPARSE did not answer")

Def XsXmlparseRead(r As XRead) As RckWork
    Select Case r
        Case XOk(tree)
            RckVals({ XcToXml(tree) })
        Case XErr(why, at)
            RckWorkBad("XMLPARSE: " & why & " AT " & Str(at))
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("XMLPARSE did not answer")

Rem ---- XMLTEXT ------------------------------------------------------------

Def XsSeedXmltext(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "XMLTEXT", 1, RckPure(Fn(vs) => RckVals({ CutStr(XmlText(XcOfXml(First(vs)))) })), "( doc -- str )", "The value, written out as XML text.")

Rem ---- XMLPRETTY ------------------------------------------------------------

Def XsSeedXmlpretty(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "XMLPRETTY", 2, RckPure(Fn(vs) => XsXmlpretty(vs)), "( doc n -- str )", "The value, written out as XML text indented n spaces per level.")

Def XsXmlpretty(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckWholeArg("XMLPRETTY", Nth(vs, 2))
        Case Ok(n)
            RckVals({ CutStr(XmlPretty(XcOfXml(Nth(vs, 1)), n)) })
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("XMLPRETTY did not answer")

Rem ---- XMLLOAD --------------------------------------------------------------

Def XsSeedXmlload(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "XMLLOAD", 1, RckTouch(Fn(vs) => XsXmlload(vs)), "( path -- doc )", "The file, read and parsed as XML — a refusal names why it could not be, whether that is the file or the syntax.")

Def XsXmlload(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckTextArg("XMLLOAD", First(vs))
        Case Ok(path)
            XsXmlloadRead(TryReadFile(path))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("XMLLOAD did not answer")

Def XsXmlloadRead(r As Result) As RckWork
    Select Case r
        Case Ok(text)
            XsXmlparseRead(XmlRead(text))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad("XMLLOAD: cannot read the file")
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("XMLLOAD: cannot read the file")

Rem ---- XMLSAVE --------------------------------------------------------------

Def XsSeedXmlsave(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "XMLSAVE", 2, RckTouch(Fn(vs) => XsXmlsave(vs)), "( path doc -- ok )", "Write the value to path as XML text; True on success.")

Def XsXmlsave(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckTextArg("XMLSAVE", Nth(vs, 1))
        Case Ok(path)
            RckVals({ CutBool(TryWriteFile(path, XmlText(XcOfXml(Nth(vs, 2))))) })
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("XMLSAVE did not answer")

Rem ---- the seed -----------------------------------------------------------

Def RckSeedXml(st As RckState) As RckState
    Let s1 = XsSeedXmlparse(RckSeeding(st, "seed-xml"))
    Let s2 = XsSeedXmltext(s1)
    Let s3 = XsSeedXmlpretty(s2)
    Let s4 = XsSeedXmlload(s3)
    XsSeedXmlsave(s4)
